#: ''Ja, '''schon'''.'' — “Yes, indeed.”

=====Usage notes=====
{{term|schon|Schon|lang=de}} is used more frequently than its English equivalents.  It is often used to emphasize agreement or the earliness of an action. With reference to time, the opposite of ''schon'' is {{term|erst|lang=de}}. While ''schon'' emphasizes how soon something will happen, ''erst'' emphasizes how long it is until something happens. Thus ''schon in drei Wochen'' means "in only three weeks [and I'm glad I don't have to wait longer!]", while ''erst in drei Wochen'' means "not for three weeks [and that seems so far away]".

